WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:11.572
Billy followed one of the elves into Santa's workshop.

2
00:00:11.573 --> 00:00:15.548
The elves were very busy packing up toys.

3
00:00:15.549 --> 00:00:20.519
Billy wanted to help, but the elves were too busy to tell him how.

4
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.584
Billy decided to go look for his father.

5
00:00:25.585 --> 00:00:30.921
He saw his father talking to Santa Claus near the reindeer stables.

6
00:00:30.922 --> 00:00:38.945
Billy didn't want to bother him, so he went into the stables instead.

7
00:00:38.946 --> 00:00:44.503
Billy had never seen reindeer before, and he thought they were very big.

8
00:00:44.504 --> 00:00:53.328
Billy looked at the biggest one and said, "Wow, you're much bigger than I thought you would be."

9
00:00:53.329 --> 00:00:58.954
The reindeer nodded and said, "Yes, many people say that."

10
00:00:58.955 --> 00:01:06.449
"Did you say something?" asked Billy. Animals aren't supposed to talk!

11
00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:10.270
"Yes, I did," said the reindeer matter-of-factly.

12
00:01:10.271 --> 00:01:14.960
"My name is Dasher. What's your name?"

13
00:01:14.961 --> 00:01:21.136
Billy understood. They were Santa's reindeer, so of course they could talk.

14
00:01:21.137 --> 00:01:25.729
"My name is Billy. Santa said you were sick.

15
00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:29.562
Are you feeling better?" he asked.

16
00:01:29.563 --> 00:01:32.437
"We're not sick," said Dasher sadly.

17
00:01:32.438 --> 00:01:39.044
"We're just really sad. We can't fly if we're sad."

18
00:01:39.045 --> 00:01:43.458
"Oh, just like Peter Pan," said Billy.

19
00:01:43.459 --> 00:01:51.603
"When he taught Wendy and the boys to fly, he said they had to think happy thoughts."

20
00:01:51.604 --> 00:01:59.974
Dasher nodded. "Yes, that's right, but it's hard to think happy thoughts when everyone is so busy.

21
00:01:59.975 --> 00:02:06.422
Santa doesn't have time for us anymore. We're lonely and we miss him."

22
00:02:06.423 --> 00:02:15.406
Billy looked at Dasher and said, "If I bring Santa in here right now, will that make you happy?"

23
00:02:15.407 --> 00:02:18.505
"Nothing can bring Santa in here on Christmas Eve.

24
00:02:18.506 --> 00:02:24.490
He's too busy," said Dasher tearfully.

25
00:02:24.491 --> 00:02:33.324
Billy didn't want to see Dasher cry, so he said, "But if I bring Santa in here, would that make you happy?"

26
00:02:33.325 --> 00:02:46.520
Dasher was sobbing quietly, so he didn't answer, but Comet, Cupid, and Vixen said, "Yes, that would make us very happy."

27
00:02:46.521 --> 00:02:51.489
Billy left the stable and ran to find his father and Santa Claus.

28
00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:56.225
He found them in Santa's workshop, looking into a microscope.

29
00:02:56.226 --> 00:03:06.860
"Well, it's not an infection," said Doctor Vinton, stepping away from the microscope.

30
00:03:06.861 --> 00:03:11.497
"I know what's wrong with the reindeer, Daddy," said Billy.

31
00:03:11.498 --> 00:03:16.862
"They're too sad to fly. It's just like Peter Pan."

32
00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:23.335
Billy's father looked at Billy and said gently, "Billy, Peter Pan is a fairy tale.

33
00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:28.605
This is real, and the problem is real."

34
00:03:28.606 --> 00:03:35.978
Santa stopped looking in the microscope and asked Billy, "Why are they sad?"

35
00:03:35.979 --> 00:03:41.728
"They're sad because you no longer have time to visit with them," said Billy.

36
00:03:41.729 --> 00:03:46.664
"They miss you and they want to see you."

37
00:03:46.665 --> 00:03:52.941
Santa turned to Billy's father and said, "Peter Pan is not a fairy tale.

38
00:03:52.942 --> 00:03:55.647
I knew Peter many years ago.

39
00:03:55.648 --> 00:04:01.189
He was such a wonderful boy, but like all boys, he grew up.

40
00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:04.462
I think Billy has solved our problem.

41
00:04:04.463 --> 00:04:13.365
If my reindeer are unhappy, they can't fly. Only happy reindeer can fly."

42
00:04:13.366 --> 00:04:18.057
Santa Claus left his workshop and went to the stables.

43
00:04:18.058 --> 00:04:24.231
Billy and his father waited. After a very long time, Santa returned.

44
00:04:24.232 --> 00:04:29.617
He was very happy. "Billy, you have saved Christmas.

45
00:04:29.618 --> 00:04:38.287
Thank you for making my reindeer happy. Ho, ho, ho!"

46
00:04:38.288 --> 00:04:42.041
Billy watched the elves load Santa's sleigh.

47
00:04:42.042 --> 00:04:50.264
Even though the elves kept putting more and more toys into the sleigh, the pile never got bigger.

48
00:04:50.265 --> 00:04:55.465
When the elves finished loading the sleigh, Santa came with his reindeer.

49
00:04:55.466 --> 00:04:59.609
Dasher came up to Billy and said, "Thank you, Billy.

50
00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:03.299
Giving Santa back to us was a wonderful Christmas present.

51
00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:07.622
I hope Santa gives you something special."

52
00:05:07.623 --> 00:05:12.193
"Oh, I'm sure he will," said Billy happily.

53
00:05:12.194 --> 00:05:19.640
As Santa and his reindeer took off, Santa shouted down to Billy, his father, and the elves:

54
00:05:19.641 --> 00:05:33.998
"Merry Christmas to all, and to all a good night! Ho, ho, ho!"
